6. NO GUARANTEE OF RESULTS
   The Software visualizes the storage usage it can read from your device.
   Displayed sizes can differ from other tools (for example because of file
   system access rights, hard links, compression, or files changing during
   a scan). You remain responsible for verifying important information
   before deleting or moving data based on what the Software displays.

7. TRIAL PERIOD, DEVICE-BOUND LICENSE FILE, AND REVOCATION
   The Software may be used in full, without a license file, for an initial
   trial period of seven (7) days, starting on first launch after
   installation. Beyond that trial period, use of the Software requires a
   valid license file that is cryptographically signed by the copyright
   holder and bound to a specific device (identified by a hashed,
   non-reversible device identifier). The Software will refuse to scan once
   the trial period has ended and no such file is present, if the file's
   signature cannot be verified, if the file was issued for a different
   device, or if the license term has ended.
   (a) Reinstalling the Software on the same device does not require a new
       license file. Moving your license to a different device requires
       contacting the copyright holder (Section 11) for reissuance.
   (b) The copyright holder may revoke or deactivate a license file at any
       time, including but not limited to cases of breach of this license
       or fraud. Where the Software performs its periodic online revocation
       check, a previously activated license remains usable for a grace
       period of up to 30 days after the Software last completed that check
       successfully (for example because the device was offline), after
       which it stops functioning until connectivity is restored or a new
       license file is issued. A license that is explicitly revoked stops
       functioning once the Software next performs a successful revocation
       check; no grace period applies to an explicit revocation.
   (c) The online check transmits only the license identifier to the
       revocation list on the official website; the Software does not
       transmit the contents of your drives.

